From: Yoni Yang <yoni980807@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 17:47:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: advertise Aurora OEM Kiwi-v2 MLO resources

Original source commit f5c689be6e603b259a5a85774d78c9cbd7cfefa4:

Add experimental Xiaomi 14 port with stock ABL boot

Build Houji kernel, userspace and internal boot images from pinned public inputs and bundled stock firmware. Include the guarded installer, device integrations, regression tests and build/flash documentation. Hide the incompatible generic installer on Houji.

The original 0013 patch is a bare diff without separate mail metadata or
sign-off/review trailers. Author/date/message above come from its source
commit. Local adaptation: rebase onto 7.3-rc5 and restrict the same resource
advertisement to Xiaomi Aurora's OEM HMT2.0 firmware. Host MLO enablement,
ring sizes and other boards retain upstream behavior.

Aurora reaches WMI service-ready but its firmware enters RDDM immediately
following WMI INIT when QMI host MLO capability is omitted. The vendor
CNSS2 Kiwi path advertises one chip, links 0/1 and max_mlo_peer=32.

Source: https://github.com/yoni13/armada-houji/blob/f5c689be6e603b259a5a85774d78c9cbd7cfefa4/ports/houji/patches/0013-ath12k-houji-stock-qmi-mlo.patch
Vendor-reference: https://github.com/OnePlusOSS/android_kernel_modules_and_devicetree_oneplus_sm8650/blob/38d50357db2728300a61b6f757f2d3a09651c155/vendor/qcom/opensource/wlan/platform/cnss2/qmi.c#L275
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/qmi.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/qmi.c
@@ -2290,6 +2290,33 @@
 	ret = ath12k_host_cap_parse_mlo(ab, &req);
 	if (ret < 0)
 		goto out;
+	/* The pinned Xiaomi Kiwi v2 firmware expects the stock CNSS topology.
+	 * Stock CNSS advertises this single-chip topology before WMI INIT.
+	 * The mobile firmware allocates max_mlo_peer - 2 entries even when
+	 * the host does not expose MLO through mac80211.
+	 */
+	if (ab->hw_rev == ATH12K_HW_WCN7850_HW20 &&
+	    of_machine_is_compatible("xiaomi,aurora")) {
+		req.mlo_capable_valid = 1;
+		req.mlo_capable = 1;
+		req.mlo_chip_id_valid = 1;
+		req.mlo_chip_id = 0;
+		req.mlo_group_id_valid = 1;
+		req.mlo_group_id = 0;
+		req.max_mlo_peer_valid = 1;
+		req.max_mlo_peer = 32;
+		req.mlo_num_chips_valid = 1;
+		req.mlo_num_chips = 1;
+		req.mlo_chip_info_valid = 1;
+		memset(req.mlo_chip_info, 0, sizeof(req.mlo_chip_info));
+		req.mlo_chip_info[0].chip_id = 0;
+		req.mlo_chip_info[0].num_local_links = 2;
+		req.mlo_chip_info[0].hw_link_id[0] = 0;
+		req.mlo_chip_info[0].hw_link_id[1] = 1;
+		req.mlo_chip_info[0].valid_mlo_link_id[0] = 1;
+		req.mlo_chip_info[0].valid_mlo_link_id[1] = 1;
+	}
+
 
 	if (ab->qmi.dynamic_ddr_support) {
 		req.dynamic_mem_support_valid = 1;
